    "reason": "The assertion that regularization 'prevents' overfitting is a guarantee rather than a possibility; however, in practice, if the regularization strength (hyperparameter) is too high, it can induce underfitting or fail to prevent overfitting if the training patterns are not the sole source of error. Thus, 'reducing reliance on specific training patterns' is a necessary mechanism but not a sufficient","counterexample": "A model with excessive L2 regularization applied to noisy data may generalize poorly (underfit) despite reduced reliance on specific training patterns, demonstrating that the condition does not guarantee prevention of overfitting in all cases.","sound_as_stated": false
  }
}
